C.F of 360 and 456 is 24. . Required greatest number is 24. Example 8. What is the greatest number which divides 57, 98 and 183 with no remainder ? Solution : Required greatest number will be the H.C.F. of 57,98 and 183. Here, 57 =3 x 19, 93 =3 x 31 and 183 =3 x 61 .. H.C.F. of 57, 93 and 183 is 3. . Required greatest number is 3. Example 9. Which is the smallest number when added by 5 the summation will be divided by 16, 24 and 32 ? Solution : The required number will be 5 less than L.C.M. of 16, 24 and 32. 16, 24, 32 8, 12, 16 , 6,8 3,4 3,2 > NNN N em] 5) Forma-3, Mathematics, Class-6 18 Mathematics “. L.C.M. of 16, 24 and 32=2x2x2x2x3x2=96 .. Required least number will be (96 — 5) or 91. Example 10: 150 227 black 401 liten; Keay \\berriers 7 UE basket 1 basket 2 basket 3 a) Determine the factors of 159 and then separate the prime factors. b) If 9 mangoes, 7 black berries and 1 litchi rotted, find out the L.C.M.',560,'06-Mathematics.pdf','tesseract','tesseract 5.3.4 -l eng, pdftoppm 200dpi gray; verbatim OCR, whitespace collapsed only; ~50-word overlap with previous chunk in same chapter; maths notation may OCR noisily, see extraction log'),
