inequality If the antecedent is smaller than the consequent of a simple ratio, the ratio is called the ratio of less inequality. For example 3 : 5and 4 : 7 both are the ratios of less inequality. In a school, the average age of the students of class III is 8 years and that of the students of class V is 10. Here, the ratio of the average ages of the students of class III and class V is 8: 100r4:5. The antecedent being smaller than the consequent, it is called the ratio of less inequality. Ratio of greater inequality If the antecedent is greater than the consequent of a simple ratio, it is called the ratio of greater inequality. Such as 5: 3, 7: 4 and 6:5 all are the ratios of greater inequality. Sadia bought a packet of biscuit for Tk.',550,'06-Mathematics.pdf','tesseract','tesseract 5.3.4 -l eng, pdftoppm 200dpi gray; verbatim OCR, whitespace collapsed only; ~50-word overlap with previous chunk in same chapter; maths notation may OCR noisily, see extraction log'),
('class6-math-en-chunk-2-004','class6-math-en','class6-math-en-ch2','en',51,53,56,58,4,'of less inequality. Ratio of greater inequality If the antecedent is greater than the consequent of a simple ratio, it is called the ratio of greater inequality. Such as 5: 3, 7: 4 and 6:5 all are the ratios of greater inequality. Sadia bought a packet of biscuit for Tk. 32 and a cone ice-cream for Tk. 25. Here, the ratio of prices of biscuit and ice-cream is 32 : 25. The antecedent 32 of this ratio being greater than the consequent 25, it is the ratio of greater inequality. Unit Ratio The ratio in which the antecedent and the consequent are equal is called unit ratio. For example, Arif bought a ballpen for Tk. 15 and a notebook for Tk.15. Here, the prices of ballpen and notebook are the same and the ratio of prices is15:15 or1: 1. So, it is unit ratio. Inverse Ratio The ratio formed by interchanging the antecedent and consequent of a simple ratio is called inverse ratio. For example, 5 : 13 is the inverse ratio of a simple ratio 13 : 5. Mixed or Compound Ratio The ratio formed by whose antecedent and consequent are formed by the products of antecedents and consequent of more than one simple ratio is called mixed or compound ratio. 52 Mathematics Such as, the mixed ratio of simple ratios 2 : 3 and 5 : 7 is (2x 5):(3x 7)=10: 21. Example 3. Determine the compound ratio of the given simple ratios 5 : 7, 4: 9, 3:2. Solution : The product of the antecedents of the given three ratios is 5x4x3=60. and the product of the subsequents is 7 x 9 x 2= 126 .. Required compound ratio is 60: 126 or 10:21. Activity : (1) (2) (3) (4) (5) Express as the inverse ratio of the simple ratio 4 : 9 Determine the antecedents and consequents of the following ratios (a)4:11 (b) 7: 5 (c) 19:21. Which one of the following is unit ratio ? (a)2:5 (b) 5:7 (c) 11:11 Divide the followings into the ratio of less inequality and the ratio of greater inequality : (a) 13:19 (b) 7: 12 (c) 25 : 13 (d) 27:7 Determine the 